# (BASIC 2.0) pictures on the text shell: sh tests/shots.sh EMU SD basic2s SECONDS (REV $0B+),
# with PREP = tests/basic2s-prep.py on the card copy.
# (0.31) Taken at states, not at times (they were at 7.0 9.0 13.0 17.5 19.5 26.5 28.5 31.0 33.5
# 36.5 s, and moved whenever the kernel or BASIC got faster or slower): basic2s-prep.py gives
# the three programs a fixed seed and makes their animations hold still after a number of
# steps; DRIFT steers by its step count. Each picture: "still 90" (the screen has not
# changed for 90 frames: the step reached, a picture drawn, BASIC waiting), then "shot".
#   1  SPRITES.BAS: balls (sprites from text art) in the graphics window, at step 110
#   2  Esc: "Break in 185", the sprites gone, the window's picture stays
#   3  DRIFT.BAS (full screen 320 x 180): its title
#   4  Space starts it; at step 150 the boat moved right and down, sprites on the river
#   5  Esc: back to the desktop, the graphics window shows the last picture
#   6  SCROLLER.BAS: full screen over a 640 x 360 world, the panel at the top, raster bands,
#      at step 120
#   7  Alt+Tab: the desktop, the program still running (its window shows the top left)
#   8  Esc (the console has the focus): Break, the BASIC window as it was
#   9  CONT, a key: the full screen again, scrolled on to step 240
#  10  Esc, SCREEN 0: the window closed, the console alone
1500 {esc}
+1500 basic -r /programs/SPRITES.BAS\n
+0 still 90
+0 shot
+100 {esc}
+0 still 90
+0 shot
+300 run /programs/drift.bas\n
# (the full screen is black, and still, for about 0.8 s while DRIFT reads its pictures;
# then the title: 90 frames)
+0 still 90
+0 shot
+300 {d2C}
+200 {u2C}
+0 still 90
+0 shot
+100 {esc}
+0 still 90
+0 shot
+300 run /programs/scroller.bas\n
# the world drawn (in sight), the panel: SCROLLER waits for a key; then the bands, and
# it scrolls to step 120 and holds (the raster bands' edges move by a line in a frame now and
# then, at random: 20 frames)
+0 still 90
+300 x
+0 still 20
+0 shot
+100 {dE2}
+100 {d2B}
+100 {u2B}
+100 {uE2}
+0 still 90
+0 shot
+300 {esc}
+0 still 90
+0 shot
+300 cont\n
+1000 x
# (the raster bands' edges move by a line in a frame now and then, at random: 20 frames)
+0 still 20
+0 shot
+100 {esc}
+1000 screen 0\n
+0 still 90
+0 shot
